WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:04.137
-Our next guest is one-third of
the Grammy-nominated band Haim.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.372
She received Golden Globe
and Critics' Choice nominations

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:09.409
for her acting debut in the
Oscar-nominated film

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:10.843
"Licorice Pizza,"
which is in theaters now.

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:12.378
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.981
-Listen, dad, he's an atheist
and an actor and he's famous!

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.015
-But he's Jewish.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.383
-He was gonna take me
out of here!

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.852
Este, don't you even look at me.
Don't you even look at me.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:21.154
You're always looking at me.
-Oh, my...

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.822
-What are you doing?
-I didn't even say anything.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.623
-What are you doing?
What are you thinking, huh?

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:26.626
"I'm Este.
I work for mom and dad.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.428
I'm perfect.
I'm a real-estate agent.

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.929
Alana doesn't have
her life together.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.765
Alana brings home stupid
boyfriends all the time."

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:34.834
-I mean...
-I knew it.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.837
-Please welcome back to the show
Alana Haim, everybody.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.773
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.687
Welcome back!

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.188
I'm so thrilled
to have you here.

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:57.890
-Thank you for having me.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:01.427
Hi, guys!
-This -- I adored this film.

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:02.728
You were fantastic in it.

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:05.598
But before we move on,
I love that clip so much because

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.434
that is your actual family...

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.001
-Oh, yeah.
-...playing your family...

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:10.202
-Yes.
-...in the film.

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:12.672
And that look
your sister gives you --

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.173
that just seems like a look
she's probably given you

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:15.174
in real life.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:16.242
-Oh, a million times.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.012
-I mean, I was
a very quiet baby sister.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.713
I, you know, stayed in my place.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.115
I never liked to rock the boat.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:25.050
And I think filming that scene
was like 30 years of me

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.622
just holding it in,
and it just erupted after that.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.524
-I guess that's a very unique
way of doing method acting is

00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:34.126
just like, "You know, it would
be great if you could get

00:01:34.126 --> 00:01:35.228
my actual family, and then --"

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:36.662
-Oh, totally.
-Yeah.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:38.164
-It's my form of therapy.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.199
-I wonder --
Because your sisters --

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.768
You know, I know they're
obviously onstage with you

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:45.371
all the time, and I know your
parents are musicians, as well,

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:48.374
but were you nervous when you
found out that your parents

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.975
were going to play
your parents in the film?

00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:51.277
Because my parents
are here all the time.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.712
They're great, but I also am
nervous having them.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:56.982
-I was so excited, because my
parents are hilarious,

00:01:56.982 --> 00:01:59.786
and I was just -- I mean, who
else could play my dad

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.020
other than my dad?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.855
Really. I don't know
who else could play my dad

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:03.923
other than my dad.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.625
Please let me know.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.493
-And what was it like
the first time?

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.796
Did you watch the film for
the first time with all of them?

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.897
-We did.
-Okay.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.965
-We all sat down
and watched it together,

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:15.068
and my parents -- The thing is,
they didn't have scripts,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.369
so they had no idea
what the movie was about.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:19.906
I tried to explain,
"There's waterbeds,

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:23.009
there's pinball machines,"
and they were trying to follow,

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.544
but didn't really understand.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:27.646
And I'll never forget,
my dad, after the movie,

00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:30.649
he just sat in silence,
and we all were like,

00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:31.684
"Dad, are you okay?

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.952
Like, what are you thinking?"

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:36.755
And he stood up in front of all
of us and went,

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:41.260
"Este, actress, 100%.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.429
Danielle, maybe.

00:02:44.429 --> 00:02:47.399
Alana, no, no, she's not.

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:48.701
How did you know, Paul?"

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.736
He, like, literally could not
understand how Paul knew

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:51.804
that I could act.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.706
He did not understand.
-So he was happy.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.441
He was blown away
with how good you were.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.010
-He was happy,
but he was just, like,

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.278
so mind-blown
that he never saw it.

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:01.881
He always wanted Este
to be the actress.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.349
I'm sorry, Este. I'm sorry.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.518
-That must --
I mean, I can't imagine.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.887
It must be fascinating as
a parent to see somebody --

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:10.789
especially a parent who's
so supportive and has known

00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:12.258
the many other talents
you have --

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.459
to see somebody else
find a talent

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.627
you didn't know
your daughter had.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:15.995
That must have been such
a cool thing for him.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:18.397
-It was -- I mean,
but he's really the star.

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:19.465
-He does steal his scenes.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.401
-I think my dad
really is the star.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.803
I mean, yeah, I'm going to
give it up to my dad.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.204
You mentioned
Paul Thomas Anderson,

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.338
the director of this film.

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:27.673
That's the Paul
you were talking about.

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:29.142
What was it like when
he first called you to ask you

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.543
to do this role?

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:35.281
-I was super-nervous, obviously,
but I'm up for adventures.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.549
I was like, "Come on,
give it to me.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.251
I want to go. I want to go.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.719
Get me in that truck.
I want to drive."

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.020
I was ready.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.855
I mean, obviously, of course,
like, I was nervous,

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.557
but I was ready to go.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:48.427
-And has this introduced you
to a new line of fans?

00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:50.096
I mean, obviously,
you have fans as a musician.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.564
Did people see this film
who maybe didn't know you

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:52.698
as a musician?

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:56.535
-I mean, you know,
I'm a, you know,

00:03:56.535 --> 00:04:00.773
young, 30-year-old, single gal,
so when you're in --

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:04.743
[ Crowd cheers ]
Thank you.

00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:06.779
So, you know,
like, what do you do

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:09.515
when you're a
young, 30-year-old, single gal?

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.550
You go on Instagram and, like,

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.386
maybe peruse your messages...

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.787
-Sure.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.090
-...just to, you know,
dabble, see maybe --

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.124
-Yeah. You were in a movie!

00:04:19.124 --> 00:04:21.527
-I was in a movie.
-Yeah.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:24.830
And, funny enough, you know
who reaches out the most?

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.033
-Who's that?
-Orthodontists.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.568
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:34.806
The world, everyone is
concerned about my teeth.

00:04:34.806 --> 00:04:40.312
I've gotten over 10 DMs
from orthodontists asking if

00:04:40.312 --> 00:04:44.617
I need help and can they
please fix my teeth?

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.686
And I love my teeth.
-Yeah!

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:50.189
-I love my teeth and I have a
snaggletooth and I'm not --

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.126
I'm very proud
of my snaggletooth.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.428
But the world of dentistry
is not pleased.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:56.762
-Yeah.

00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:59.666
Well, this breaks their heart,
because the worst outcome

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:03.435
from them is that someone can
succeed despite their help.

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:04.704
-I know. Exactly.

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:07.206
-But you did --
I mean, as a survivor of

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:09.808
orthodonture myself --
I had a long run.

00:05:09.808 --> 00:05:10.843
I had about
five years in braces.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.278
You did have braces.

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:16.915
-I had braces for four years,
and this is what my teeth --

00:05:16.915 --> 00:05:20.186
I don't know if you can,
like, zone in on my teeth,

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:22.755
but this is what
my teeth look like.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:26.392
Like -- Oh, it's happening.
It's happening. Come on.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:30.062
Come on, come on.
-There we go. Those are great.

00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:32.865
Those are very --
Those are the only teeth that

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.133
could have been in this role.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:37.369
But you sent us
a photo of yourself

00:05:37.369 --> 00:05:38.570
in braces to prove this.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.706
And the best thing about
this photo --

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:41.807
Because it's a
birthday picture.

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:43.342
-It is. It's my 13th birthday.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:45.478
-The best thing is what you got
for your 13th birthday.

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:47.779
-It was the best thing ever.

00:05:47.779 --> 00:05:50.916
I got "The O.C." box set.

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:53.852
Look how happy I am.

00:05:53.852 --> 00:05:55.054
"The O.C." box set.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.589
My mom got it from Costco,

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.224
and it was the best day
of my life.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:02.227
I cried, and you can see
I'm nervous even holding it.

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:03.696
I don't even think I opened it.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.431
-Yeah.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:08.934
This is, of course --
This film is about

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:11.303
the youth of California,
but it's the Valley,

00:06:11.303 --> 00:06:14.340
and it's such a --
You mentioned, like,

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.508
you know,
it takes place in the '70s,

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:17.410
and it is, like,
waterbeds and pinballs.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.145
You had to learn
how to drive a truck...

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.313
-Yes.

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:23.115
-...which I -- You know,
with all apologies to

00:06:23.115 --> 00:06:24.917
Tom Holland, that truck scene

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:28.053
was the best action scene
in any film this year.

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:29.355
-You said it.
-Yeah, there you go.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:31.624
I said it.
-I'm not saying a word.

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:33.425
I'm taking your word for it.

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:37.096
-What is the difference between
acting on film

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:39.698
that you found versus
being onstage?

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:41.466
Because, obviously,
that's a performance, as well.

00:06:41.466 --> 00:06:42.668
-You know, it's funny.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.971
When I perform with my band,
Haim, like,

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:49.275
five minutes before the show,
I regret my whole life.

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:51.176
I pace around.

00:06:51.176 --> 00:06:52.744
I pace around, I go,
"What am I doing?

00:06:52.744 --> 00:06:53.980
How do I --
Why do I do this to myself?

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.347
Like, I can't go out there."

00:06:55.347 --> 00:06:58.650
I have incredible stage fright.
Like, I am so nervous.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:01.153
And then the second that I step
onstage, there's like a veil,

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:03.556
and I'm just like a new person.

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:05.458
And filming "Licorice Pizza,"

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.227
I feel like five minutes before,
like, while we were

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:09.262
setting up a shot, I'd be like,
"Oh, my God.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.263
I can't do this.

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:11.697
I can't do this.
I can't do this."

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:14.433
And then Paul would call action,
and I'd be like, "I'm ready."

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:16.668
And it was the same,
and it was great.

00:07:16.668 --> 00:07:18.003
-Are your sisters the same way?

00:07:18.003 --> 00:07:19.905
Do you guys all have the same,
like, nerves pre-show

00:07:19.905 --> 00:07:21.406
or is it different
for all three of you?

00:07:21.406 --> 00:07:22.541
-I feel like it's definitely --

00:07:22.541 --> 00:07:24.042
I mean, I never know
Danielle's pre-show,

00:07:24.042 --> 00:07:25.110
because she doesn't talk.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.379
-Okay, gotcha.

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:29.815
-And if you're a Haim fan,
you know what I mean.

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:32.485
No, I love my sister. No. No.

00:07:34.152 --> 00:07:36.155
No, I mean, we all kind of
have our own things,

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:37.189
but we're so -- I mean,

00:07:37.189 --> 00:07:39.024
we're incredibly excited
to go on tour.

00:07:39.024 --> 00:07:42.528
I cannot wait to finally go on
tour and play our latest album.

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:43.929
-And this is the biggest tour
you've ever done.

00:07:43.929 --> 00:07:44.997
-Biggest tour.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.332
We're playing
Madison Square Garden.

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:48.167
-It's unbelievable.
-It's crazy.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.502
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It's unbelievable.

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:53.472
You might have to
give yourself 10 minutes

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:54.573
to pace before that one.

00:07:54.573 --> 00:07:57.276
-Oh, yeah.
No, that's like a full 24 hours.

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:58.477
Full 24 hours.

00:07:58.477 --> 00:07:59.511
-That's thrilling
and so exciting.

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:00.680
And you're actually --

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:01.681
You're going to do
something cool tonight.

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:02.948
-Yes.

00:08:02.948 --> 00:08:06.819
-We are going to do
a giveaway to a Haim fan...

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:08.320
-Yes.
-...that is in the audience.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:09.788
But you're going to go --
We're going to send you

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:12.992
to the audience to ask
a trivia question.

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.626
And here's the only thing
we'll ask is,

00:08:14.626 --> 00:08:15.895
if you think you have
the answer,

00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:17.262
don't just raise your hand.

00:08:17.262 --> 00:08:19.899
Also stand up so it's easier
for Alana to find you.

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:20.933
-Yes.
-Alright, get out there.

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:22.334
-So, am I going?
-Let's go. Get out there.

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:26.305
-Okay, let's do it. Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:29.809
Okay.

00:08:32.811 --> 00:08:35.181
Hi, guys!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:37.849 --> 00:08:40.419
Yay! Okay.

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:42.521
Wait. So, do --
Should I ask if there are --

00:08:42.521 --> 00:08:43.589
if there is --

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:45.090
-Alright, yeah,
so, let's do this.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:48.594
So, first, do you think you can
answer a question about Haim?

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:50.329
-You stand up.
What is your name?

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:52.097
-Annie.
-Annie.

00:08:52.097 --> 00:08:54.534
Let's give it up for Annie.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:03.075
Annie, I will ask you
this question.

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:06.245
Can you name three Haim songs?

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:08.480
-Yes.
-Number one.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.816
-Yes. "The Wire."
-Boom! Got it.

00:09:10.816 --> 00:09:12.585
Number two.
-"My Song 5."

00:09:12.585 --> 00:09:14.719
-Boom! Number three.
-"Something to Tell You."

00:09:14.719 --> 00:09:15.821
-Hey!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.761
Annie!

00:09:22.761 --> 00:09:24.396
-Alana!

00:09:24.396 --> 00:09:27.366
-Okay, you got it!
-Alana, tell them what they won!

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:29.368
-I got to tell you what you won.
Are you ready?

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:30.702
-Yes!

00:09:30.702 --> 00:09:35.308
-You won two tickets to any
Haim show that you want

00:09:35.308 --> 00:09:38.077
on the "One More Haim" tour.

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:40.512
And wait. There's more, guys.

00:09:40.512 --> 00:09:43.081
There is more.

00:09:43.081 --> 00:09:44.417
Airfare.

00:09:46.618 --> 00:09:50.422
And two nights in a hotel!

00:09:50.422 --> 00:09:52.991
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:52.991 --> 00:09:57.797
Annie...I love you.

00:09:57.797 --> 00:10:01.667
I love you. I love her.
I love her.

00:10:01.667 --> 00:10:04.970
-You guys,
give it up for Alana Haim.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.839
"Licorice Pizza"
is in theaters now.

00:10:06.839 --> 00:10:08.907
And for information on
the "One More Haim" tour,

00:10:08.907 --> 00:10:10.609
visit haimtheband.com

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:12.078
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

